From: Joel Gerber <Jitsusama@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] Give the block allocator a bin for each size up to 2 KB

Qt 6.12.0's block allocator keeps freed runs in eight bins by their
size in 32-byte slots, the last holding every run of seven slots or
more. A request of seven or more walks that list from its head for a
run large enough, passing each too small, and walks it again whenever
the run it split runs out. The shell's last bin held 10,000 to 84,000
runs as it started, and perf put 84% of a 4 s stall at its start in
that walk. Requests under 63 slots now have a bin of their own size,
so the last holds only runs that fit nearly anything; a request for it
passes at most 32 runs too small before taking a new chunk, which the
next sweep sorts back into the bins.

---
--- a/src/qml/memory/qv4mm.cpp
+++ b/src/qml/memory/qv4mm.cpp
@@ -448,9 +448,14 @@ HeapItem *BlockAllocator::allocate(size_t size, bool forceAllocation) {
         goto done;
     }
 
-    // search last bin for a large enough item
+    // search last bin for a large enough item, passing at most a few too small, since each pass
+    // of a long list is paid again by every request that follows it
     last = &freeBins[NumBins - 1];
-    while ((m = *last)) {
+    for (size_t tries = 0; (m = *last); ++tries) {
+        if (tries == LargeBinTries) {
+            m = nullptr;
+            break;
+        }
         if (m->freeData.availableSlots >= slotsRequired) {
             *last = m->freeData.next; // take it out of the list
 
--- a/src/qml/memory/qv4mm_p.h
+++ b/src/qml/memory/qv4mm_p.h
@@ -178,7 +178,13 @@ struct BlockAllocator {
         memset(freeBins, 0, sizeof(freeBins));
     }
 
-    enum { NumBins = 8 };
+    // A bin for each size up to 2 KB, so the last one holds only runs that fit nearly anything
+    // asked of it. With eight, every request of 224 bytes or more walked one list of every free
+    // run that size or larger, passing each too small for it.
+    enum { NumBins = 64 };
+
+    // How many runs too small a request for the last bin passes before it takes a new chunk.
+    enum { LargeBinTries = 32 };
 
     static inline size_t binForSlots(size_t nSlots) {
         return nSlots >= NumBins ? NumBins - 1 : nSlots;
